`∫_s (f − f̄)² ≤ ω⁻¹ ∫_s ∫_s (f(x) − f(y))² dy dx`, `f̄ = ω⁻¹ ∫_s f` (both sides vanish if
`ω = 0`).  For each `x`, `f(x) − f̄ = ω⁻¹ ∫_s (f(x) − f(y)) dy`, so Cauchy–Schwarz
